update public.publications set venue = '2026 8th International Congress on Human-Computer Interaction, Optimization and Robotic Applications (ICHORA) · IEEE', publication_date = '2026', status = 'Published · IEEE Conference Paper', authors = 'Anas Mahyoub Naji Saeed Alqadhi; Mohammed Ali Mohammed S. Bajhaw; Munef el Muhammed; Aysegul Ucar', doi = '10.1109/ICHORA69329.2026.11537209', summary = 'A drift-resilient LiDAR–IMU mapping system for GPS-denied indoor environments, integrating RKO-LIO with a Velodyne VLP-16 and Pixhawk Cube Orange+ under ROS 2.', details = $abstract$Indoor 3D mapping in GPS-denied environments requires drift-resilient LiDAR–IMU fusion to ensure geometric consistency over extended trajectories. This work integrates a Velodyne VLP-16 3D LiDAR and a Pixhawk Cube Orange+ IMU on a TurtleBot Waffle Pi running ROS 2 Humble, and evaluates RKO-LIO, a LiDAR–inertial odometry method that avoids sensor-specific modeling via a physics-based kinematic motion model with adaptive scan-to-map regularization. Geometric accuracy is validated against roll-meter ground-truth measurements across five indoor test objects, achieving an RMSE of 0.026 m, MAE of 0.022 m, and mean error of 0.69% (range: 0.03% to -1.47%). A controlled simulation comparison replays an identical sensor bag through RKO-LIO, LIO-SAM, and FAST-LIO in three Gazebo indoor environments. FAST-LIO achieves the lowest trajectory error in all scenes; LIO-SAM is accurate in feature-rich environments but diverges catastrophically in the bookstore scene (APE 21.7 m, map destroyed); RKO-LIO produces bounded-error trajectories across every environment (APE ≤0.494 m) without per-scene parameter tuning. These results demonstrate that worst-case robustness—not peak accuracy—is decisive for real GPS-denied indoor deployment.$abstract$, keywords = array['LiDAR–IMU Fusion','Indoor 3D Mapping','GPS-Denied Environments','RKO-LIO','ROS 2','SLAM','Drift Resilience','Simulation Benchmarking'], url = '/manus-storage/rko-lio-velodyne-pixhawk-ros2-paper_01b4facc.pdf', sort_order = 1 where id = 1; with project_record as (insert into public.projects (slug, title, subtitle, summary, description, status, tags, tools, outcomes, featured, sort_order, publication_url) values ('rko-lio-indoor-3d-mapping-platform', 'RKO-LIO Indoor 3D Mapping Platform', 'A real-robot LiDAR–IMU mapping system validated in GPS-denied indoor environments.', 'An end-to-end ROS 2 platform that fuses Velodyne LiDAR and Pixhawk IMU data for resilient indoor 3D mapping, then benchmarks robustness against alternative odometry pipelines.', $description$This project implements and evaluates an indoor 3D mapping platform for environments where GPS is unavailable. The real-robot stack integrates a Velodyne VLP-16 LiDAR, Pixhawk Cube Orange+ IMU, TurtleBot Waffle Pi base, and ROS 2 Humble data flow to generate consistent spatial maps from LiDAR–inertial measurements.

The engineering work focused on deploying RKO-LIO, a sensor-agnostic LiDAR–inertial odometry pipeline built around a kinematic motion model and adaptive scan-to-map regularisation. The system was tested against roll-meter measurements across five indoor objects and benchmarked by replaying the same sensor bag through RKO-LIO, LIO-SAM, and FAST-LIO inside three Gazebo worlds.

The final evaluation demonstrates centimetre-level geometric fidelity on the real platform, while the simulation study exposes the practical reliability trade-off between peak trajectory accuracy and bounded error under difficult mapping conditions. The accompanying IEEE paper documents the experimental design, quantitative results, and full comparison.$description$, 'Published research project', array['LiDAR–IMU Fusion','RKO-LIO','ROS 2','Indoor 3D Mapping','GPS-Denied','SLAM'], array['ROS 2 Humble','RKO-LIO','Velodyne VLP-16','Pixhawk Cube Orange+','TurtleBot Waffle Pi','Gazebo','rosbag Replay'], array['0.026 m RMSE and 0.022 m MAE against roll-meter ground truth','0.69% mean dimensional error across five indoor test objects','Bounded RKO-LIO error across all three Gazebo environments (APE ≤0.494 m)','13.7× improvement over a prior LIO-SAM deployment on identical hardware'], true, 0, 'https://doi.org/10.1109/ICHORA69329.2026.11537209') on conflict (slug) do update set title = excluded.title, subtitle = excluded.subtitle, summary = excluded.summary, description = excluded.description, status = excluded.status, tags = excluded.tags, tools = excluded.tools, outcomes = excluded.outcomes, featured = excluded.featured, sort_order = excluded.sort_order, publication_url = excluded.publication_url returning id), media_data(storage_path, alt, sort_order) as (values ('/manus-storage/rko-paper-figure-000_006a4407.jpg', 'Hardware platform with Velodyne VLP-16, Jetson AGX Orin, Pixhawk Cube Orange+, custom housing, and OpenCR card', 1), ('/manus-storage/rko-paper-figure-002_f4dad55c.jpg', 'Indoor point-cloud reconstruction and roll-meter validation across five test objects', 2)) insert into public.project_media (project_id, storage_path, alt, sort_order) select project_record.id, media_data.storage_path, media_data.alt, media_data.sort_order from project_record cross join media_data where not exists (select 1 from public.project_media existing_media where existing_media.project_id = project_record.id and existing_media.storage_path = media_data.storage_path);
